thon\ncright[-right.shape[0]:, -right.shape[1]:] = right\n```\nThis copies the sub-matrix itself, the same way the left-hand side is already handled.\n\n`separability_matrix(m.Pix2Sky_TAN() & cm)` now returns:\n```\n[[ True  True False False]\n [ True  True False False]\n [False False  True False]\n [False False False  True]]\n```\n\nThe suggested pytest command doesn't work as given in this environment. It picks up the installed astropy instead of the repo copy, and fails before any tests run. To get the tests to run I added `PYTHONPATH=.`, turned off the `astropy_header` plugin and ignored deprecation warnings, from the repo root:\n```\nPYTHONPATH=. python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -p no:astropy_header -W ignore::DeprecationWarning astropy/modeling/tests/test_separable.py\n```","ttft_ms":2354,"type":"result","duration_ms":30349,"uuid":"51bfd122-3973-4fbb-89f9-c314b1a21ff0","ttft_stream_ms":1980,"time_to_request_ms":64,"first_content_frame_ms":1980,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":14,"outputTokens":1643,"cacheReadInputTokens":125595,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12244,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.155987,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":62,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":12244,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
